WEBVTT

00:22:26.829 --> 00:22:30.038
But, you know, I have personally
felt like, you know,

00:22:30.038 --> 00:22:34.746
working with people who don't look like
you, especially when they are, you know,

00:22:34.746 --> 00:22:41.246
smart and freethinkers. It's incredible
how much better the conversation is,

00:22:41.246 --> 00:22:43.871
how much richer it is, and I think how
much better the work ends up being.

00:22:44.163 --> 00:22:48.579
And I'm grateful for any time I work with
someone, whether it's Matt, Latoya,

00:22:48.579 --> 00:22:54.288
I can name a huge list of people who are
really willing to rethink things that

00:22:54.288 --> 00:22:57.246
I might just assume need to stay.

00:22:57.496 --> 00:22:59.246
And the only caveat I would
say here is that

00:22:59.246 --> 00:23:04.038
I can also think of times when there
were paths we were on and